8service100の93記録、326044 raw到着について予定(worker,sequence)を復元し、保存則と348個のread\/write対の窓の件数・分位点を独立再計算。不一致0。疎な実メソッド窓とforce_primary回復writeの未着手1件は残る。旧壁時計窓の却下も保持されており、いずれもサービスSLO合格へ変換していない。","初期\/最終58表のexpected\/actualとreplica20000000行を独立照合。owner quiescenceのINNODB_TRX=0、fixture利用者なし、matrix不在を確認。最終撤去exitCode=0、完全ログ results\/reviews\/owner-essential-final-cleanup.log SHA-256=ec3db27786327db1d56189a4d844fa8e9f2c4b7a0ea74941e0e0122c6a535722。現在.data不在。時計修正検証もexitCode=0、完全ログ results\/reviews\/author-clock-repair-verification.log SHA-256=fc99e1d8b9565d257c9b2795f7c8ccf2a606b57055559ddb4f22e1f29516cc3e。","finding-register.json SHA-256=c239cfc99d9ae377e3b138a005fa1ab5cdebd82e0d708d6c733f08343345b68dと、その8原レビューのハッシュを照合。除外gridは測定成功へ数えていない。本受入れは現revision25の文書と限定された証跡に対する最終reviewer2判定であり、本番SLO・普遍的精度・物理隔離・全条件最速の認定ではない。"],"reviewQuestions":{"betterMethods":"精度・鮮度・予算別の選択は妥当。承認済みエクスポートを優先し、参考統計と経験的校正を区別する。必須精度には資源を隔離した取得先の既定COUNTを候補とし、標本は全適用条件を満たす場合だけ比較する。primary現在値の常時計数は、更新・再試行・移行等の整合を扱う別設計としている。","designCoverage":"未知のPK・索引、整数PKなし、欠番・偏在、NULL、LOB、50\/100列TDE、アプリseedなし、更新中、partition・シャード・世代違いをたどり、安全な取得先または保留へ分岐できた。標本適格性はSQL上の一意整数PKで判断し、暗号化の由来では判断しない。VIEW・非InnoDBは自動投入せず所有者確認へ戻す。100M×80列×TDEへの外挿もしていない。","fastCount":"既存索引の既定COUNTを候補にする判断は[公式COUNT仕様](https:\/\/dev.mysql.com\/doc\/refman\/8.4\/en\/aggregate-functions.html)と整合する。旧・新105の小比較中央値は原JSONから一致し、COUNT一文と標本SQL開始〜ROLLBACKの計測区間差、cache・read-ahead・順序・host層の未制御を踏まえている。取消COUNTを完了速度にせず、標本未達をUNKNOWNとする。普遍的最速、行数だけの安全閾値、一般的な精度保証や無影響は主張しておらず、現推薦の判断に不可欠な追加測定はない。","lockFactors":"通常のInnoDB RC\/RR SELECTは行非ロックだが、MDL・長いread view・undo保持・資源競合は残るという説明は妥当。[整合性読取](https:\/\/dev.mysql.com\/doc\/refman\/8.4\/en\/innodb-consistent-read.html)と[MDL仕様](https:\/\/dev.mysql.com\/doc\/refman\/8.4\/en\/metadata-locking.html)に照合した。索引選択を行ロック発生と混同せず、EXPLAINも安全証明にしていない。locking read、DML\/CTAS\/SET埋込み、SERIALIZABLE、意図的競合注入の追加要求は不要。","omissions":"現推薦を妨げる実務上の欠落は認めない。SQL前の取得先・予算・監視と新規専用接続、統計cache miss\/expiry\/既存expiry=0、UNKNOWN処理、準備作業のprimary負荷、共有資源の隔離・上限、GTID\/復元位置・鮮度を扱う。事前・実行中・回復監視、別の取消経路、停止余裕、現在のjob所有権照合、サーバー処理終了確認、盲目的再試行禁止も開始条件になっている。[公式KILL仕様](https:\/\/dev.mysql.com\/doc\/refman\/8.4\/en\/kill.html)の非同期終了とも整合する。準備できなければ保留する。"},"revision":25,"workflowInput":{"acceptanceCriteriaPath":"results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json","currentRevision":25,"detailPaths":["docs\/probability-count.md","audit\/README.md"],"historyReference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json","reproductionProofPath":"results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json","reviewPaths":["docs\/table-count-guideline.md","docs\/table-count-calibration.md","README.md"],"scopePath":"bench\/nonlocking-scope.json"}},"when":{"accepted":true}},"adapterOutput":{"completionPassed":true,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","provider":"codex","when":{"accepted":true}},"attempt":1,"backend":"codex-agent","backendEventCount":5,"backendWorkingDirectory":"\/Users\/taco\/gits\/tacogips\/database-analysis","createdAt":"2026-11-07T16:44:47Z","executionId":"review-attempt-1-exec-67","inputSnapshot":{"_rielaHistoryContract":{"inputDigest":"e43304cdc38fad600ef0e54f337923da0abc1a1d827c172c97a60a708bf448b6","payloadDigest":"e81b1bd956bfd7eb1eacaf5125695c913c755970313298ee41be294fd6d6cf40","variablesDigest":"a4ca907fe0646ca516e6b1aa48575456aab99316e5844eff06802ebea3d105dd","workflowDigest":"58c801e8d984510daa35c725f40b8c6dd840daed913f5da4fc7d6e8e2a87bc63"},"arguments":{"calibrationPath":"docs\/table-count-calibration.md","calibrationSha256":"99bfd0477a19c4cf1f0f60967aa37957073ae6283d68f959979bc72669cf61a0","discussionHistory":[{"meaning":"Historical scope; current user priority and actual operational claims govern materiality. Not automatic technical closure.","reference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json"}],"firstReviewPath":"results\/reviews\/final-engineer-review-result.json","guidelinePath":"docs\/table-count-guideline.md","guidelineSha256":"0d0680c03caf17e9e36524d051f0247e0e9f77fe7ac7d0298289c6cdf673f5b5","reproductionProofSha256":"0ef235cd8832593093b25335121253fae8ab2fc5c2bf9feb1384c30ba2e93350","revision":25,"workflowInput":{"acceptanceCriteriaPath":"results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json","currentRevision":25,"detailPaths":["docs\/probability-count.md","audit\/README.md"],"historyReference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json","reproductionProofPath":"results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json","reviewPaths":["docs\/table-count-guideline.md","docs\/table-count-calibration.md","README.md"],"scopePath":"bench\/nonlocking-scope.json"}},"freshPromptText":"You are GPT-6.1 Sol only, final reviewer2: adversarial-validation-and-operations, and the final review gate. Use a NEW session separate from author\/integrator and reviewer1. You are read-only: no writes, DB\/Docker\/benchmarks, state-changing commands, delegation, workflow calls, commit or push. Read-only file\/hash\/syntax inspection and official documentation checks are allowed.\n\nCurrent authority and scope:\n- The latest user prioritizes an unfamiliar engineer obtaining counts for their own huge MySQL service without degradation. Give a usable decision and explicit deferral; never promise universal zero impact or a globally fastest algorithm.\n- Read AGENTS.md, results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json and owner-operator-guide-open-checks.json first. Read runtimeVariables\/workflowInput as provided; preserve workflowInput and revision in schema outputs. Use the actual current guide and linked calibration, not a historical draft.\n- bench\/nonlocking-scope.json is the exact current allowlist\/exclusion ledger. Keep ordinary InnoDB RC\/RR plain SELECT, reference statistics, conditional sampling, TDE\/plain SELECT, and normal service-write load. Ordinary SELECT still takes MDL; fixture maintenance and business UPDATE\/INSERT\/DELETE have separate natural locks. Non-InnoDB is quiet catalog only.\n- Do not restore or request FOR SHARE\/FOR UPDATE, COUNT embedded in DML\/CTAS\/SET, LOCK TABLES\/FTWRL, SERIALIZABLE COUNT, or intentional pending-DDL\/FLUSH\/ANALYZE contention injection. Broad engine\/scale\/write-mix and duplicate width grids explicitly skipped by the user are superseded_by_explicit_user_scope, not measurement passes, technical closure, or missing current default coverage.\n- Preserve historical findings by references and stable IDs in results\/reviews\/finding-register.json and its source reviews. Reassess material operational concerns against the current recommendation. Do not copy giant historical adapters or force every old grid to run. Author submissions and owner audits are not independent reviewer closure.\n\nPerform your own review of current guide\/calibration and raw immutable evidence FIRST, without anchoring on reviewer1. Challenge causal, accuracy and operational safety claims: cache\/read-ahead\/order and host layers, actual index path versus EXPLAIN, TDE server keys versus client seed\/ciphertext, restored statistics versus old production cache, replica\/backup provisioning and shared resources, MDL\/undo\/cancellation, arrival conservation and sparse\/censored windows. Scope limitations must be explicit; do not expand the grid to investigate claims the guide does not make.\n\nEvidence and final gate:\n- Read results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json, final-all-candidate.json, the candidate's complete log and fixed measurementSnapshot manifest. Read every owner audit referenced by proof, including semantic\/source, integrity, precision\/budget, runtime quiescence and cleanup. Hash the current guide and linked current detail documents. Verify the supplied guidelineSha256, not an earlier revision's digest.\n- Verify proof measurementSnapshot.manifestSha256 and every manifest file; verify candidatePath\/candidateSha256, fresh runnerSummary, process numeric exit, source-before=after=current for the complete source set, scope hash and pinned image identities. Verify the owner bundle manifest hash and every referenced report\/source hash. The archived verification-source\/README.md is historical documentation; allowed current docs edits do not waive any measurement\/auditor source mismatch. Verify the seven public Python audit sources remain at proof hashes. A static planned_not_db_executed scope label is not runtime status.\n- Candidate collection or exit0 alone is not owner acceptance. Missing\/inconsistent proof, source drift, unexplained semantic failures, incomplete logs or unconfirmed cleanup remain incomplete. Never invent owner acceptance, retrofit timestamps, silently promote reused\/failed\/unknown-exit evidence, or accept at a round\/time limit.\n- Bind every quoted result to a hash-verified immutable source. Separate old observations, rejected wall-clock windows and the new monotonic run; do not overwrite historical claims with new figures. Check fresh metadata93, encrypted91, static105 and service48 for counterexamples. Counts\/accuracy may be valid while service windows are invalid. Preserve all tied minima, exact signed\/absolute errors, rounded zero versus exact zero, and rejected prototype estimates (including 100% error\/UNKNOWN).\n- Distinguish experimental completion, precision achieved, service\/resource budget and cleanup. Timed\/cancelled COUNT is not a completed count or completion speed. Preserve unfinished\/unstarted arrivals, sparse\/censored tails, and actual-method versus broad windows. Process success does not prove service SLO, cache parity, causal ranking, universal accuracy or physical production isolation.\n\nOperational acceptance checks:\nWalk the guide as an engineer with an unfamiliar huge encrypted table, unknown statistics, no application seed, 50\/100 columns, possibly no dedicated replica and limited permissions. Check:\n1. First use approved existing inventory\/monitoring exports. Before any scoped SQL establish target, owner budget\/monitoring and a NEW dedicated connection, never an application pool\/transaction. Nonzero stats_expiry is not cache-only; missing\/expired cache or existing expiry=0 can fetch engine stats. No extra primary impact allowed\/no budget means exported stats, isolated acquisition or explicit deferral. NULL\/zero\/uninitialized\/denied\/missing\/error is not certified empty.\n2. Rough statistics, empirically calibrated estimates, conditional probabilistic bounds and exact snapshot counts are separate. A few representative tables do not prove a universal bound. Logical restoration\/rebuild changes page layout\/statistics; compare matching generation\/time and never transfer restored-statistics error to old production cache. Approximate smallness never authorizes unbounded primary COUNT.\n3. Provisioning replicas\/backups itself can load primary: require approved owner-budgeted procedures. Establish resource isolation\/caps before monitoring; dedicated\/shared replica labels alone are insufficient. Define freshness\/GTID\/restore position, missing shards and generations. No compliant target means defer or relax precision\/freshness explicitly.\n4. Pre\/during\/post monitoring and a named cancellation owner with a separate control path; stop thresholds with detection\/cancel headroom BEFORE SLO violation. A SQL timeout is insufficient prevention. Match current query ownership using job tag, target\/account and start context plus connection ID; never KILL a recycled ID blindly. Confirm server work\/read view ended and service recovery, and forbid blind retry.\n5. Supported InnoDB RC\/RR plain SELECT COUNT(*) is row-nonlocking but has MDL\/undo\/resource costs; locking DML and SERIALIZABLE are separate excluded forms. No long pooled\/shared transaction, automatic primary ANALYZE\/index creation, or automatic replica stop. COUNT(col) drops NULLs; COUNT(1) is no magic acceleration.\n6. TDE server key availability differs from client seed\/application ciphertext. SQL-visible integer PK eligibility is structural, not determined by encryption provenance. No extrapolation from thin100M or750k50\/100-column synthetic TDE to100M80-column production performance. Existing-index\/default COUNT may beat sampling; conditional sampling needs all snapshot\/PK\/randomness\/cell-bound\/stopping\/confidence\/budget\/cleanup criteria, not stable repeats alone.\n7. Lab preflight recommendation labels and legacy research docs are diagnostics\/history, not production permission or current mandatory experiment plans. The guide must be usable without running this lab.\n\nAnswer all five schema keys in reviewQuestions, even with no findings:\n- betterMethods: Is an available simpler option better for the specified precision\/freshness\/budget (existing exported stats, calibrated stats, default COUNT with existing index, isolated target, conditional sampling, or a separately designed maintained counter)? Explain only decision-relevant alternatives and their load\/lock\/prerequisites; do not enumerate every imaginable engine feature.\n- designCoverage: Does routing give a safe answer or explicit deferral for unknown PK\/index, gaps, wide\/LOB\/TDE, nullable columns, churn, partitions\/shards\/generations and non-InnoDB\/views outside this procedure? Test representative failure cases; do not require every design crossed with every state.\n- omissions: Identify actionable operational prerequisites, freshness\/permissions, UNKNOWN\/error handling, provisioning impact, monitoring\/cancellation\/recovery and no-compliant-path handling. Distinguish actual defects from explicitly scoped limitations.\n- lockFactors: Verify ordinary RC\/RR InnoDB SELECT versus excluded locking forms, unavoidable MDL and long read-view\/resource costs. Index choice changes work but does not make plain SELECT acquire row locks. EXPLAIN is not a locking\/safety certificate. Do not demand excluded lock-injection experiments.\n- fastCount: Does the guide choose a justified efficient option for the requested accuracy and freshness without unsupported safety\/fastest claims? Check the small immutable COUNT\/sample comparison, measurement intervals, calibration eligibility and unsupported production extrapolation. No universal ranking or row-count-only safety threshold.\n\nMeasurement requests:\nRaise additional measurements ONLY if indispensable to decide a specific remaining operational recommendation. State that recommendation, the concrete counterexample, why existing evidence\/official semantics are insufficient, and what decision each possible result changes. Prefer correcting\/removing an unsupported recommendation or explicitly marking it unmeasured when that fully resolves the defect. Do not turn every measurable question or table design into a grid. Do not run DB\/Docker\/benchmarks, delegate or invoke workflows in this session. A necessary unresolved measurement stays pending for the owner; it is never a pass. Do not waive actual high\/middle defects to avoid measurement.\n\nReport real defects, not style preferences. Each finding: stable id, severity high\/middle\/low, section, concrete scenario\/counterexample, source file\/field or official URL, operational impact and required correction. Real high\/middle defects and necessary pending experiments block acceptance. An explicitly unmeasured condition is not automatically a defect if the guide safely defers or withholds that recommendation.\nUse findingDispositions to retain stable IDs and source references for material historical concerns: verified_fixed, still_open, disputed_with_evidence, or superseded_by_explicit_user_scope. The last category is never a technical pass. Review actual corrections rather than trusting author labels; never assert another review closed a finding without its artifact.\n\nThen inspect reviewer1 (unfamiliar-service-engineer) independently. For each first-review finding, record confirm\/reject with concrete evidence in independentFindingAssessment and pass findings through independentFindings. An unsupported\/out-of-scope first-review objection need not block; a confirmed high\/middle does. If reviewer1 was rejected, acceptance requires explicit evidence-based rejection of every blocking objection and any indispensable measurement request; otherwise reject. Missing\/mismatched reviewer1 revision or digest is incomplete.\n\nReturn {\"when\":{\"accepted\":BOOL},\"payload\":{...}} with accepted=the same BOOL, decision=accepted\/rejected consistently, workflowInput, revision, guidelinePath, guidelineSha256, reviewQuestions (all five), findings, independentFindings, independentFindingAssessment, findingDispositions, requestedExperiments, reviewEvidence and discussionHistory.\nSet true ONLY if this current revision and linked detail hashes were fully reviewed, strict final owner proof\/source\/artifact\/cleanup checks pass, no own or confirmed reviewer1 high\/middle finding is open, and no indispensable experiment remains. Never accept at a round limit or from process success, scope skip, or an author\/owner summary alone.\n\nFinal operational review. Read results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json. Do not run DB\/Docker, mutate state, delegate or start workflows. Act as an adversarial operations\/validation reviewer. Review the guide yourself FIRST; only then open firstReviewPath and assess its findings with evidence. Verify the actual current guide and calibration hashes and owner proof. No unsupported global safety\/accuracy claim; no resurrected exhaustive grids. Return the required SMALL adapter with actual evidence, not copied historical adapters.","mergedVariables":{"_rielaInput":{"communicationIds":[],"messages":[],"sourceStepIds":[],"stepId":"review","workflowExecutionId":"temp-final-count-validation-sol-session-34"},"availableMemories":{"node":[],"workflow":[]},"calibrationPath":"docs\/table-count-calibration.md","calibrationSha256":"99bfd0477a19c4cf1f0f60967aa37957073ae6283d68f959979bc72669cf61a0","discussionHistory":[{"meaning":"Historical scope; current user priority and actual operational claims govern materiality. Not automatic technical closure.","reference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json"}],"firstReviewPath":"results\/reviews\/final-engineer-review-result.json","guidelinePath":"docs\/table-count-guideline.md","guidelineSha256":"0d0680c03caf17e9e36524d051f0247e0e9f77fe7ac7d0298289c6cdf673f5b5","memoryCommandHelp":"","nodeId":"review","nodeKind":"worker","reproductionProofSha256":"0ef235cd8832593093b25335121253fae8ab2fc5c2bf9feb1384c30ba2e93350","revision":25,"runtimeVariables":{"_rielaInput":{"communicationIds":[],"messages":[],"sourceStepIds":[],"stepId":"review","workflowExecutionId":"temp-final-count-validation-sol-session-34"},"calibrationPath":"docs\/table-count-calibration.md","calibrationSha256":"99bfd0477a19c4cf1f0f60967aa37957073ae6283d68f959979bc72669cf61a0","discussionHistory":[{"meaning":"Historical scope; current user priority and actual operational claims govern materiality. Not automatic technical closure.","reference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json"}],"firstReviewPath":"results\/reviews\/final-engineer-review-result.json","guidelinePath":"docs\/table-count-guideline.md","guidelineSha256":"0d0680c03caf17e9e36524d051f0247e0e9f77fe7ac7d0298289c6cdf673f5b5","reproductionProofSha256":"0ef235cd8832593093b25335121253fae8ab2fc5c2bf9feb1384c30ba2e93350","revision":25,"workflowInput":{"acceptanceCriteriaPath":"results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json","currentRevision":25,"detailPaths":["docs\/probability-count.md","audit\/README.md"],"historyReference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json","reproductionProofPath":"results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json","reviewPaths":["docs\/table-count-guideline.md","docs\/table-count-calibration.md","README.md"],"scopePath":"bench\/nonlocking-scope.json"}},"workflowDescription":"Final separate Sol operational review: validation","workflowId":"temp-final-count-validation-sol","workflowInput":{"acceptanceCriteriaPath":"results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json","currentRevision":25,"detailPaths":["docs\/probability-count.md","audit\/README.md"],"historyReference":"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json","reproductionProofPath":"results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json","reviewPaths":["docs\/table-count-guideline.md","docs\/table-count-calibration.md","README.md"],"scopePath":"bench\/nonlocking-scope.json"}},"promptText":"You are GPT-6.1 Sol only, final reviewer2: adversarial-validation-and-operations, and the final review gate. Use a NEW session separate from author\/integrator and reviewer1. You are read-only: no writes, DB\/Docker\/benchmarks, state-changing commands, delegation, workflow calls, commit or push. Read-only file\/hash\/syntax inspection and official documentation checks are allowed.\n\nCurrent authority and scope:\n- The latest user prioritizes an unfamiliar engineer obtaining counts for their own huge MySQL service without degradation. Give a usable decision and explicit deferral; never promise universal zero impact or a globally fastest algorithm.\n- Read AGENTS.md, results\/reviews\/third-party-engineer-acceptance.json and owner-operator-guide-open-checks.json first. Read runtimeVariables\/workflowInput as provided; preserve workflowInput and revision in schema outputs. Use the actual current guide and linked calibration, not a historical draft.\n- bench\/nonlocking-scope.json is the exact current allowlist\/exclusion ledger. Keep ordinary InnoDB RC\/RR plain SELECT, reference statistics, conditional sampling, TDE\/plain SELECT, and normal service-write load. Ordinary SELECT still takes MDL; fixture maintenance and business UPDATE\/INSERT\/DELETE have separate natural locks. Non-InnoDB is quiet catalog only.\n- Do not restore or request FOR SHARE\/FOR UPDATE, COUNT embedded in DML\/CTAS\/SET, LOCK TABLES\/FTWRL, SERIALIZABLE COUNT, or intentional pending-DDL\/FLUSH\/ANALYZE contention injection. Broad engine\/scale\/write-mix and duplicate width grids explicitly skipped by the user are superseded_by_explicit_user_scope, not measurement passes, technical closure, or missing current default coverage.\n- Preserve historical findings by references and stable IDs in results\/reviews\/finding-register.json and its source reviews. Reassess material operational concerns against the current recommendation. Do not copy giant historical adapters or force every old grid to run. Author submissions and owner audits are not independent reviewer closure.\n\nPerform your own review of current guide\/calibration and raw immutable evidence FIRST, without anchoring on reviewer1. Challenge causal, accuracy and operational safety claims: cache\/read-ahead\/order and host layers, actual index path versus EXPLAIN, TDE server keys versus client seed\/ciphertext, restored statistics versus old production cache, replica\/backup provisioning and shared resources, MDL\/undo\/cancellation, arrival conservation and sparse\/censored windows. Scope limitations must be explicit; do not expand the grid to investigate claims the guide does not make.\n\nEvidence and final gate:\n- Read results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json, final-all-candidate.json, the candidate's complete log and fixed measurementSnapshot manifest. Read every owner audit referenced by proof, including semantic\/source, integrity, precision\/budget, runtime quiescence and cleanup. Hash the current guide and linked current detail documents. Verify the supplied guidelineSha256, not an earlier revision's digest.\n- Verify proof measurementSnapshot.manifestSha256 and every manifest file; verify candidatePath\/candidateSha256, fresh runnerSummary, process numeric exit, source-before=after=current for the complete source set, scope hash and pinned image identities. Verify the owner bundle manifest hash and every referenced report\/source hash. The archived verification-source\/README.md is historical documentation; allowed current docs edits do not waive any measurement\/auditor source mismatch. Verify the seven public Python audit sources remain at proof hashes. A static planned_not_db_executed scope label is not runtime status.\n- Candidate collection or exit0 alone is not owner acceptance. Missing\/inconsistent proof, source drift, unexplained semantic failures, incomplete logs or unconfirmed cleanup remain incomplete. Never invent owner acceptance, retrofit timestamps, silently promote reused\/failed\/unknown-exit evidence, or accept at a round\/time limit.\n- Bind every quoted result to a hash-verified immutable source. Separate old observations, rejected wall-clock windows and the new monotonic run; do not overwrite historical claims with new figures. Check fresh metadata93, encrypted91, static105 and service48 for counterexamples. Counts\/accuracy may be valid while service windows are invalid. Preserve all tied minima, exact signed\/absolute errors, rounded zero versus exact zero, and rejected prototype estimates (including 100% error\/UNKNOWN).\n- Distinguish experimental completion, precision achieved, service\/resource budget and cleanup. Timed\/cancelled COUNT is not a completed count or completion speed. Preserve unfinished\/unstarted arrivals, sparse\/censored tails, and actual-method versus broad windows. Process success does not prove service SLO, cache parity, causal ranking, universal accuracy or physical production isolation.\n\nOperational acceptance checks:\nWalk the guide as an engineer with an unfamiliar huge encrypted table, unknown statistics, no application seed, 50\/100 columns, possibly no dedicated replica and limited permissions. Check:\n1. First use approved existing inventory\/monitoring exports. Before any scoped SQL establish target, owner budget\/monitoring and a NEW dedicated connection, never an application pool\/transaction. Nonzero stats_expiry is not cache-only; missing\/expired cache or existing expiry=0 can fetch engine stats. No extra primary impact allowed\/no budget means exported stats, isolated acquisition or explicit deferral. NULL\/zero\/uninitialized\/denied\/missing\/error is not certified empty.\n2. Rough statistics, empirically calibrated estimates, conditional probabilistic bounds and exact snapshot counts are separate. A few representative tables do not prove a universal bound. Logical restoration\/rebuild changes page layout\/statistics; compare matching generation\/time and never transfer restored-statistics error to old production cache. Approximate smallness never authorizes unbounded primary COUNT.\n3. Provisioning replicas\/backups itself can load primary: require approved owner-budgeted procedures. Establish resource isolation\/caps before monitoring; dedicated\/shared replica labels alone are insufficient. Define freshness\/GTID\/restore position, missing shards and generations. No compliant target means defer or relax precision\/freshness explicitly.\n4. Pre\/during\/post monitoring and a named cancellation owner with a separate control path; stop thresholds with detection\/cancel headroom BEFORE SLO violation. A SQL timeout is insufficient prevention. Match current query ownership using job tag, target\/account and start context plus connection ID; never KILL a recycled ID blindly. Confirm server work\/read view ended and service recovery, and forbid blind retry.\n5. Supported InnoDB RC\/RR plain SELECT COUNT(*) is row-nonlocking but has MDL\/undo\/resource costs; locking DML and SERIALIZABLE are separate excluded forms. No long pooled\/shared transaction, automatic primary ANALYZE\/index creation, or automatic replica stop. COUNT(col) drops NULLs; COUNT(1) is no magic acceleration.\n6. TDE server key availability differs from client seed\/application ciphertext. SQL-visible integer PK eligibility is structural, not determined by encryption provenance. No extrapolation from thin100M or750k50\/100-column synthetic TDE to100M80-column production performance. Existing-index\/default COUNT may beat sampling; conditional sampling needs all snapshot\/PK\/randomness\/cell-bound\/stopping\/confidence\/budget\/cleanup criteria, not stable repeats alone.\n7. Lab preflight recommendation labels and legacy research docs are diagnostics\/history, not production permission or current mandatory experiment plans. The guide must be usable without running this lab.\n\nAnswer all five schema keys in reviewQuestions, even with no findings:\n- betterMethods: Is an available simpler option better for the specified precision\/freshness\/budget (existing exported stats, calibrated stats, default COUNT with existing index, isolated target, conditional sampling, or a separately designed maintained counter)? Explain only decision-relevant alternatives and their load\/lock\/prerequisites; do not enumerate every imaginable engine feature.\n- designCoverage: Does routing give a safe answer or explicit deferral for unknown PK\/index, gaps, wide\/LOB\/TDE, nullable columns, churn, partitions\/shards\/generations and non-InnoDB\/views outside this procedure? Test representative failure cases; do not require every design crossed with every state.\n- omissions: Identify actionable operational prerequisites, freshness\/permissions, UNKNOWN\/error handling, provisioning impact, monitoring\/cancellation\/recovery and no-compliant-path handling. Distinguish actual defects from explicitly scoped limitations.\n- lockFactors: Verify ordinary RC\/RR InnoDB SELECT versus excluded locking forms, unavoidable MDL and long read-view\/resource costs. Index choice changes work but does not make plain SELECT acquire row locks. EXPLAIN is not a locking\/safety certificate. Do not demand excluded lock-injection experiments.\n- fastCount: Does the guide choose a justified efficient option for the requested accuracy and freshness without unsupported safety\/fastest claims? Check the small immutable COUNT\/sample comparison, measurement intervals, calibration eligibility and unsupported production extrapolation. No universal ranking or row-count-only safety threshold.\n\nMeasurement requests:\nRaise additional measurements ONLY if indispensable to decide a specific remaining operational recommendation. State that recommendation, the concrete counterexample, why existing evidence\/official semantics are insufficient, and what decision each possible result changes. Prefer correcting\/removing an unsupported recommendation or explicitly marking it unmeasured when that fully resolves the defect. Do not turn every measurable question or table design into a grid. Do not run DB\/Docker\/benchmarks, delegate or invoke workflows in this session. A necessary unresolved measurement stays pending for the owner; it is never a pass. Do not waive actual high\/middle defects to avoid measurement.\n\nReport real defects, not style preferences. Each finding: stable id, severity high\/middle\/low, section, concrete scenario\/counterexample, source file\/field or official URL, operational impact and required correction. Real high\/middle defects and necessary pending experiments block acceptance. An explicitly unmeasured condition is not automatically a defect if the guide safely defers or withholds that recommendation.\nUse findingDispositions to retain stable IDs and source references for material historical concerns: verified_fixed, still_open, disputed_with_evidence, or superseded_by_explicit_user_scope. The last category is never a technical pass. Review actual corrections rather than trusting author labels; never assert another review closed a finding without its artifact.\n\nThen inspect reviewer1 (unfamiliar-service-engineer) independently. For each first-review finding, record confirm\/reject with concrete evidence in independentFindingAssessment and pass findings through independentFindings. An unsupported\/out-of-scope first-review objection need not block; a confirmed high\/middle does. If reviewer1 was rejected, acceptance requires explicit evidence-based rejection of every blocking objection and any indispensable measurement request; otherwise reject. Missing\/mismatched reviewer1 revision or digest is incomplete.\n\nReturn {\"when\":{\"accepted\":BOOL},\"payload\":{...}} with accepted=the same